IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory): the definitions that sit inside the in-scope sections ("In this section:", "In this chapter:", "In subsection (3):" and the like).
--
-- One constant for each definition, written by a script that reads the text file.
-- Each constant holds the term, the form of the definition, where the text says it applies, the first line as printed and the further lines as printed.
-- The definitions of the dictionary are in `act-dictionary.l4`.
-- The text is the unofficial plain-text rendering deposited with this encoding, not the authorised republication.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): definitions inside sections`

-- src:207 | law—see section 107 (Definitions—ch 11).
@ref s 15 (3), definition of law (src:207-207)
GIVETH A `Definition`
`s 15 (3), definition of law` MEANS
    `Definition` WITH
        `term` IS "law"
        `how it is defined` IS `a signpost definition`
        `applies to` IS "this section"
        `meaning as printed` IS "law—see section 107 (Definitions—ch 11)."
        `further lines as printed` IS EMPTY

-- src:229 | former Commonwealth enactment means a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or Imperial Act that is—
-- src:230 | (a) an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34; or
-- src:231 | (b) an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3).
@ref s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment (src:229-231)
GIVETH A `Definition`
`s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment` MEANS
    `Definition` WITH
        `term` IS "former Commonwealth enactment"
        `how it is defined` IS `means`
        `applies to` IS "this section"
        `meaning as printed` IS "former Commonwealth enactment means a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or Imperial Act that is—"
        `further lines as printed` IS LIST ("(a) an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34; or"), ("(b) an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3).")

